## About the standard

ISO 45001 describes how an organization can establish a management system to prevent work-related injury and ill health. It applies to organizations of different sizes and activities.

The system covers leadership, worker participation, hazard identification, occupational health and safety risks, and performance review. Certification can demonstrate that the system has been audited, but does not replace applicable legal duties.

Official source: [ISO 45001:2018](https://www.sis.se/en/produkter/environment-health-protection-safety/occupational-safety-industrial-hygiene/iso-450012018/).

